.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt DSA_DO_SIGN 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm DSA_do_sign ,
.Nm DSA_do_verify
.Nd raw DSA signature operations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/dsa.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft DSA_SIG *
.Fo DSA_do_sign
.Fa "const unsigned char *dgst"
.Fa "int dlen"
.Fa "DSA *dsa"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DSA_do_verify
.Fa "const unsigned char *dgst"
.Fa "int dgst_len"
.Fa "DSA_SIG *sig"
.Fa "DSA *dsa"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify_init 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify 3 .
.Pp
.Fn DSA_do_sign
computes a digital signature on the
.Sy len
byte message digest
.Fa dgst
using the private key
.Fa dsa
and returns it in a newly allocated
.Vt DSA_SIG
structure.
.Pp
.Xr DSA_sign_setup 3
may be used to precompute part of the signing operation in case
signature generation is time-critical.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_do_verify
verifies that the signature
.Fa sig
matches a given message digest
.Fa dgst
of size
.Sy len .
.Fa dsa
is the signer's public key.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn DSA_do_sign
returns the signature, NULL on error.
.Fn DSA_do_verify
returns 1 for a valid signature, 0 for an incorrect signature and -1 on
error.
The error codes can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr DSA_new 3 ,
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr RAND_bytes 3 ,
.Xr DSA_SIG_new 3 ,
.Xr DSA_sign 3
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
